From 2f07ac0447418482996a3b483f603b2400f83430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Edoardo Pauletto <104910976+EdoardoPauletto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:31:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add a WebSocket server for ws-scrcpy

Run as `app_process / com.genymobile.scrcpy.Server <version> web [logLevel]
[port] [listenOnAllInterfaces]` to serve the ws-scrcpy browser client
directly over WebSocket, like the NetrisTV fork of scrcpy 1.19 did.

Each stream reuses the regular pipeline (ScreenCapture or NewDisplayCapture,
SurfaceEncoder, Controller) and is shared by all the clients watching the
same display. A stream may create a new virtual display (displayId -1),
optionally resized by the client (flex display), and keep the device
active. The device audio is captured once (raw PCM) for the clients
which enable it.

Upstream changes are kept minimal:
 - Streamer: optional Sink instead of a file descriptor
 - ControlChannel: may be subclassed
 - SurfaceEncoder: encoding settings can be changed without releasing
   the capture (keeps a new virtual display alive)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
